  "content": {
    "id": "v2-a3909-p37-practice-slot-8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the stationary point on $f(x)=(x-1)^3+4$ and determine its nature.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Horizontal point of inflection at $(1,4)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=3(x-1)^2\\\\3(x-1)^2&=0\\\\x&=1\\\\f(1)&=0+4=4\\\\f''(x)&=6(x-1)\\\\f''(1)&=0\\\\f''(0)&=-6,\\qquad f''(2)=6\\end{align*}$$\nSince $f''(x)$ is negative for $x<1$ and positive for $x>1$, the concavity changes from down to up at $x=1$. Also, $f'(1)=0$, so $(1,4)$ is a horizontal point of inflection.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
